CM ============================================================
CM  TM-SC-NEC-008: Screwdriver Antenna — 60m Band
CM  2.4m whip, base loading coil, 4 horizontal elevated radials
CM  Frequency: 5.300–5.360 MHz (5 points, 0.015 MHz step)
CM
CM  Loading coil (series RL at base, segment 1 of GW1):
CM    R = 4.546 ohm  (Rcoil = Xant / Q, Q~260)
CM    X = 1182 ohm   (XL required to resonate 2.4m whip on 60m)
CM
CM  Whip: 2.4m, avg radius 0.006m, 20 segments
CM  Radials: 4 x 2.4m at z=0.005m, 90 deg spacing
CM  Ground: real (Sommerfeld-Norton), eps=13, sigma=0.005
CM  Feed: 1V voltage source at GW1, seg 1
CM
CM  Tuning note: 60m (5 MHz region) has channelized allocations
CM  in many ITU regions; check local band plan. US allocation:
CM  5330.5, 5346.5, 5357.0, 5371.5, 5403.5 kHz (USB, 2.8kHz each).
CM  FR sweep set for 5.300-5.360 MHz to cover primary channels.
CM  Heavy loading; Rcoil (4.55 ohm) exceeds Rrad at this frequency.
CM  Expect ~40% or lower efficiency. NVIS potential at this band.
CM  Ground quality strongly affects near-field losses at 60m.
CM ============================================================
